============================================================================
4. TEOREMA B's Jensen step
============================================================================

 |A_n(c)| = |sum_K b_K(c)(phi_n^{(K)}-phi_K)| <= (a/n) E[sqrt(Bin(n,c/n))]
          <= (a/n) sqrt(E[Bin(n,c/n)]) = (a/n) sqrt(c).
 sqrt is concave so Jensen goes the right way (E sqrt X <= sqrt E X).
 CORRECT given (U'_a).  Numerically E sqrt(Bin) vs sqrt(c):
   n=  100 c=   1   E sqrt(Bin) =   0.7745096513   sqrt(c) =            1.0   OK
   n=  100 c=  10   E sqrt(Bin) =    3.124847276   sqrt(c) =     3.16227766   OK
   n=  100 c=  50   E sqrt(Bin) =    7.062144434   sqrt(c) =    7.071067812   OK
   n= 1000 c= 200   E sqrt(Bin) =    14.13504855   sqrt(c) =    14.14213562   OK
